@* Routes, not panels — each face of a card is its own url, so these are links that happen to look
   like tabs rather than a tab container with content in it. `NavLink` marks the current one, which
   keeps "which tab am I on" out of C# entirely. *@
<nav class="cardtabs">
    <NavLink class="tab" href="@Href(CardSurface.Task)" Match="NavLinkMatch.All">
        @Strings.Card_Surface_Task
    </NavLink>
    <NavLink class="tab" href="@Href(CardSurface.Terminal)" Match="NavLinkMatch.All">
        @Strings.Card_Surface_Terminal
    </NavLink>
    <NavLink class="tab" href="@Href(CardSurface.Timeline)" Match="NavLinkMatch.All">
        @Strings.Card_Surface_Timeline
    </NavLink>
</nav>
